# Supabase project the portfolio's data-backed sub-apps use (travel, finance).
#
# These are the PUBLIC anon credentials — they are safe to expose in a browser
# bundle, and the same pair is already hardcoded in drunk/components/*.tsx.
# What actually protects data is row-level security in Supabase, not secrecy of
# this key: the fin_* tables revoke `anon` entirely and check owner = auth.uid().
#
# Copy to .env before building. Without them src/lib/supabase.ts creates a client
# pointed at an empty URL and every query fails.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
